<title>POLAND: POLISH OFFICIAL RESERVES RISE TO $17.85 BLN IN NOV.</title>
<headline>POLISH OFFICIAL RESERVES RISE TO $17.85 BLN IN NOV.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish official foreign currency</p>
<p>reserves grew by $146 million in November to $17.85 billion and</p>
<p>were $3.62 billion higher than a year ago, the National Bank of</p>
<p>Poland said.</p>
<p>It said official reserves grew $2.883 billion in the</p>
<p>January-November period compared to a $8.19 billion rise in the</p>
<p>corresponding period of last year.</p>
<p>    POLISH RESERVES (bln dlrs)    NOV 96    OCT 96     NOV 95</p>
<p>    Official reserves		 17.85	17.70	14.22</p>
<p>    Net reserves			21.46	21.60	19.40</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves</p>
<p>are those held by the state. Net reserves mean the total amount</p>
<p>of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
